Proposed (11.4s): Use this to add continuous evaluation and regression testing to any LLM component in the AgentsFramework agent monorepo. Triggers when you need to: instrument a component so failures don't regress silently, build a judge or rubric to score quality, set up drift detection or alerts when metrics slide, freeze production failures into CI benchmarks (must-accept/must-reject fixtures), catch regressions in the build instead of three weeks later, score or monitor a specific component (summarizer, plan_builder, router, output_validation, guardrail_validator, etc.), or close the loop from "we fixed this bug" to "it can never break again without CI failing". Covers the full path: read failures → build taxonomy → ship deterministic checks + offline regression tests → optionally add a sampled judge + drift loop. Even if the user just says "the summarizer keeps dropping action items" or "I want to make sure validation quality doesn't slide", treat it as a probe/eval request.

